                <pb facs="0578" n="488" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg488"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Stam, John C./25: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-01-03T10:00:00+08:00">January 3, 1935—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 3—5:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3. Reference Legation’s 606, December 30, noon, concerning Stam case. Peck
                    reports that he made oral representations to the Minister for Foreign Affairs on
                    December 31. The Minister expressed his grief at the terrible tragedy and
                    described measures being taken to suppress the Communists. Kuangson Young was
                    instructed to assist in arrangements for the funeral and to represent the
                    Chinese Government.</p>
                <p>I have addressed formal note to the Foreign Office dated January 2nd along the
                    line suggested in Department’s 397, December 28, 4 p.m. amended to conform with
                    recent information and Atcheson’s report.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
